WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:14.936
Life at Patty's Place continued pleasantly enough.

2
00:00:14.937 --> 00:00:23.589
The nights grew cold, but on Friday evenings, the big living room was warm and crowded with guests, laughing and talking until late at night.

3
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.912
Gilbert came occasionally on Friday evenings.

4
00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:36.640
He always seemed to have a good time, but he spoke to Anne politely, the way a new friend would. Their old camaraderie was gone entirely.

5
00:00:36.641 --> 00:00:41.250
One rainy winter's day, Anne was leaving Redmond to go home.

6
00:00:41.251 --> 00:00:45.822
The wind suddenly blew strongly, turning her umbrella inside out.

7
00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:53.460
Anne was clutching at it frantically when a voice close to her said, "Pardon me, may I offer you the shelter of my umbrella?"

8
00:00:53.461 --> 00:01:03.744
Anne looked up. A tall, handsome man with dark, melancholy eyes—the hero of Anne's dreams—stood before her.

9
00:01:03.745 --> 00:01:06.213
"Thank you," Anne said.

10
00:01:06.214 --> 00:01:10.535
"Let's hurry over to that little building," suggested the stranger.

11
00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:13.469
"We can wait there until this shower is over."

12
00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.937
The man's words were very ordinary, but his voice! And his smile!

13
00:01:18.938 --> 00:01:24.542
Anne felt her heart beating strangely. They hurried to the building.

14
00:01:24.543 --> 00:01:33.271
The raindrops sparkled on Anne's shining hair. Her cheeks were flushed, and her eyes big and starry.

15
00:01:33.272 --> 00:01:38.169
The man looked at her admiringly, and Anne blushed under his gaze.

16
00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:46.990
"We are schoolmates, I see," he said, indicating Anne's jacket with the school crest. "My name is Roy Gardner."

17
00:01:46.991 --> 00:01:51.252
"Sorry, but I don't recognize you," said Anne frankly.

18
00:01:51.253 --> 00:01:56.752
"I studied at Redmond for two years," Roy said, "and then I went to Europe.

19
00:01:56.753 --> 00:02:00.976
I've come back to do the last year of my arts degree."

20
00:02:00.977 --> 00:02:04.496
Roy walked Anne home to Patty's Place.

21
00:02:04.497 --> 00:02:08.915
Before he left, he arranged to visit Anne the following Friday.

22
00:02:08.916 --> 00:02:13.816
Later that evening a box arrived at Patty's Place for "Miss Shirley."

23
00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:18.006
It contained a dozen magnificent red roses.

24
00:02:18.007 --> 00:02:23.892
Phil impertinently read the card. "Roy Gardner!" she exclaimed.

25
00:02:23.893 --> 00:02:29.117
"Why, Anne, I didn't know you were acquainted with Roy Gardner!"

26
00:02:29.118 --> 00:02:33.383
"I met him this afternoon in the rain," explained Anne.

27
00:02:33.384 --> 00:02:38.470
"My umbrella turned inside out and he came to my rescue with his."

28
00:02:38.471 --> 00:02:49.293
"Oh." Phil looked suspiciously at Anne. "And so, naturally, he sent you roses! I smell romance!"

29
00:02:49.294 --> 00:02:56.569
"Nonsense!" Anne replied stiffly. But she lay awake a long time that night thinking about Roy.

30
00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.614
Perhaps her prince had come at last.

31
00:03:00.615 --> 00:03:04.608
Over the next few months, Anne and Roy became a couple.

32
00:03:04.609 --> 00:03:09.963
Roy came to Patty's Place every Friday night, and Gilbert stopped coming.

33
00:03:09.964 --> 00:03:14.063
Roy and Anne went to all the college events and parties together.

34
00:03:14.064 --> 00:03:22.569
He regularly sent her flowers and was always sure to murmur a poetic compliment whenever he took her hand or helped her with her coat.

35
00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:27.824
Spring came and the girls at Patty's Place were dressing for the Redmond Spring Dance.

36
00:03:27.825 --> 00:03:31.259
Anne looked at herself in the mirror with satisfaction.

37
00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.248
She had a particularly pretty gown on.

38
00:03:34.249 --> 00:03:44.160
Originally it had been only a simple chiffon dress, but Phil had embroidered tiny rosebuds all over the chiffon and now it was simply stunning.

39
00:03:44.161 --> 00:03:49.252
Anne was trying to fasten a little gold chain around her neck when Phil came in.

40
00:03:49.253 --> 00:03:55.989
"By the way, Anne, Gilbert Blythe has been seen constantly with Christine Stuart. Did you know?"

41
00:03:55.990 --> 00:04:00.865
Suddenly Anne's fingers didn't work, and she couldn't put the necklace on.

42
00:04:00.866 --> 00:04:07.209
"No, I hadn't heard," she said carelessly. "Who is Christine Stuart?"

43
00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:10.885
"Christine Stuart transferred to Redmond this semester.

44
00:04:10.886 --> 00:04:15.343
She studied music at a university in Toronto," Phil replied.

45
00:04:15.344 --> 00:04:21.052
"I haven't seen her, but they say she's very pretty and that Gilbert is quite crazy over her.

46
00:04:21.053 --> 00:04:24.082
I was so angry when you refused Gilbert, Anne!

47
00:04:24.083 --> 00:04:30.731
But Roy Gardner was meant for you. I can see that now. You were right, after all."

48
00:04:30.732 --> 00:04:35.084
Anne suddenly felt dull, and Phil's chatter seemed trivial.

49
00:04:35.085 --> 00:04:40.862
At the dance Anne danced many times with Roy, but she was acutely conscious of Gilbert.

50
00:04:40.863 --> 00:04:45.784
He stood across the room, talking to a girl who must have been Christine Stuart.

51
00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:53.117
She was lovely, with a pale complexion, long dark hair, and rosy red lips.

52
00:04:53.118 --> 00:04:57.904
Anne was not sorry when the evening ended, and everyone went home.

53
00:04:57.905 --> 00:05:02.405
Phil and Anne made hot chocolate and stayed up late discussing the night.

54
00:05:02.406 --> 00:05:06.514
"All of Redmond knows that Roy is crazy about you, Anne!

55
00:05:06.515 --> 00:05:10.983
And you've been going out for nearly six months now!" said Phil candidly.

56
00:05:10.984 --> 00:05:14.174
"You're going to marry Roy, aren't you?"

57
00:05:14.175 --> 00:05:18.129
"Phil, he hasn't even asked me!" Anne said.

58
00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.695
"You do love him, don't you, Anne?" Phil asked.

59
00:05:21.696 --> 00:05:32.487
"I . . . I . . . suppose so." Anne realized she was confessing her love for Roy for the first time. But strangely, she felt stiff inside.

60
00:05:32.488 --> 00:05:39.792
Why had her face gone red that evening every time she'd seen Gilbert Blythe and Christine Stuart together?

61
00:05:39.793 --> 00:05:43.544
After Phil went to bed, Anne thought about Roy.

62
00:05:43.545 --> 00:05:47.634
"Of course, I love him. Roy is my ideal.

63
00:05:47.635 --> 00:05:54.490
Who could resist those glorious dark eyes, his melancholic voice, his handsome looks?"

64
00:05:54.491 --> 00:05:58.379
Anne knew that half the girls at Redmond were envious of her.

65
00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.934
And Roy had written poems for her!

66
00:06:00.935 --> 00:06:07.167
Admittedly, he did copy them from magazines, but they were good poems, and very romantic!

67
00:06:07.168 --> 00:06:16.038
Anne began thinking about Gilbert. Gilbert, she knew, would never write her poems, but on the other hand, Gilbert would always understand a joke.

68
00:06:16.039 --> 00:06:23.243
The day before, Anne had told Roy a very funny story, but he had only smiled politely and didn't laugh.

69
00:06:23.244 --> 00:06:31.568
Anne recalled telling Gilbert the same story a long time ago and both of them laughing about it for ages.

70
00:06:31.569 --> 00:06:36.666
Anne wondered uneasily if life with a man who had no sense of humor might be boring.

71
00:06:36.667 --> 00:06:43.978
But who could expect a handsome, melancholy, romantic hero who wrote her poems to see the funny side of things?

72
00:06:43.979 --> 00:06:58.060
It was too much to ask! Anne put thoughts of Gilbert out of her head, and went to sleep dreaming of Roy's dark, soulful eyes.
